/**
@page editor_guide Mercury Editor Guide

@tableofcontents

The Mercury Editor is the graphical tool for making projects. It edits the
same text files the engine loads (`.mproj`, `.mmap`, `.masset`, `.uxml`,
`.minput`), so you can commit those files and diff them like code. The editor
is documented at the C++ level starting at
@ref Mercury::EditorUI::MercuryEditorApp.

@section editor_launch Opening the editor

@code{.sh}
# open a project at its main map
bazelisk run //editor:mercury_editor -- examples/pong/pong.mproj

# open a project at a specific map
bazelisk run //editor:mercury_editor -- examples/pong/pong.mproj --map res://maps/main.mmap

# open the project launcher
bazelisk run //editor:mercury_editor
@endcode

The launcher shows recent projects, an **Open** button for a `.mproj` or a
folder, drag-and-drop from the OS, and a **New Project** card. A new project
gets a `.mproj`, a main map, `scripts/`, `assets/` and a `.gitignore` that
keeps `.mercury/` out of version control. Pick **2D** for sprites and
orthographic play, or **3D** for a camera, sun, ground plane and cube.

The menus are:

| Menu | Commands |
|---|---|
| **File** | New Map, Open Map, Save, Save Map As, Set Current Map as Main Map, Build Game, Preferences, Close Project, Exit |
| **Edit** | Undo, Redo, Duplicate, Delete |
| **GameObject** | Empty Node, 3D Object, Light, 2D Sprite, Camera |
| **Project** | Build Scripts (F7), Play / Stop (F5) |
| **Script** | Go to Method, Find, Replace |
| **Window** | Toggle every panel, pop out the UI Builder and Input Actions, camera preview, reset layout |

@section editor_panels The panels

@subsection editor_hierarchy Hierarchy

The **Hierarchy** lists the current map's nodes as a tree. Select a node to
show it in the **Inspector** and the **Scene Viewport**. The **Create**
button adds an empty object, a 3D primitive (cube, sphere, capsule, cylinder,
plane or quad), a light (directional, point, area or probe volume), a 2D
sprite or a camera. Right-click a node to add a child or delete it. Drag to
re-parent; the parent's transform is applied when the map runs.

@subsection editor_inspector Inspector

The **Inspector** edits the selected node:

- **Transform** position, rotation (Euler degrees) and scale.
- Every component on the node, with typed widgets for numbers, colors, node
  references, asset references and arrays.
- **Add Component** adds a built-in component or a `[script]` class from the
  project.
- Script fields marked `[field]` appear here, with their tooltips. Fields
  marked `[nodeRef]`, `[asset "Material"]`, `[enum ...]` and `[callable]`
  get purpose-built editors.
- **Event** fields get a list editor for choosing another object, one of its
  `[callable]` methods and the argument. This is Mercury's UnityEvent.

Changes are written to the map when you save. Undo and redo are in the
**Edit** menu.

@subsection editor_scene Scene Viewport

The scene viewport draws the map with the same renderer the game uses.

| Action | 2D | 3D |
|---|---|---|
| Select | Click an object | Click an object |
| Move / rotate / scale | Drag, or W / E / R handles | Drag, or W / E / R handles |
| Snap | Hold Ctrl while dragging | Hold Ctrl while dragging |
| Frame selection | F | F |
| Pan | Right or middle drag | Middle drag |
| Zoom | Mouse wheel | Mouse wheel |
| Look | -- | Right drag (W/A/S/D/Q/E to fly, Shift for speed) |
| Orbit | -- | Alt + left drag |

The **2D** button forces the 2D view for a map whose camera is 3D, and the
camera preview window renders through the selected camera. If the viewport is
slow, releasing the mouse stops the high-rate viewport timer and the editor
returns to its normal 60 fps timer.

@subsection editor_project Project Browser

The **Project Browser** shows the project folder. Double-click a `.as` file
to open it in the script editor, a `.uxml` file to open the UI Builder, a
`.minput` file to open the Input Actions editor, or a map to open it.

The **Create** button creates:

- **Script...** -- a new `[script] class Name : Behaviour` in `scripts/`;
- **Map...** -- a new map in `maps/`;
- **Material**, **Physics Material** and **Input Actions**;
- **UI Toolkit > UI Document** (`.uxml`), **Style Sheet** (`.uss`) and
  **Panel Settings**;
- folders.

@subsection editor_script Script Editor

Double-click a `.as` file to edit it in the built-in editor. It provides line
numbers, code folding, AngelScript completion for the project and the native
API, compiler-backed error squiggles, an outline for jumping between methods,
find/replace and optional Vim keybindings. **Script > Go to Method** lists the
methods in the open file.

The editor compiles the project's scripts in **Build Scripts** and **Play**.
A compile error is shown in the **Console** and the build fails, so the game
is not started with broken scripts. The editor does not run game code itself;
it runs `mercury_player --dump-schema` to learn the scripts' fields for the
Inspector.

To use another editor, open **File > Preferences...** and set an external
editor command. `{project}` and `{file}` in the command are replaced with the
project root and the selected file.

@subsection editor_console Console

The **Console** collects engine messages, script output and errors. Each line
has a level (info, warning, error) and the panel can filter them. Clicking a
line that names a script location such as `scripts/ball.as:42:5` opens that
file at the line in the script editor.

@subsection editor_ui_builder UI Builder

**Window > UI Builder** (or double-click a `.uxml` file) edits player-facing
UI visually. It shows the document tree, a control library, the style sheets
and selectors, and an Inspector for attributes, classes, bindings and styles.
The canvas is rendered by the engine, with a preview mode, so what you see is
what the game draws. Create documents and style sheets with **Create > UI
Toolkit > UI Document (.uxml)** / **Style Sheet (.uss)**.

@subsection editor_input_actions Input Actions

**Window > Input Actions** (or double-click a `.minput` file) edits Unity-style
input actions: action maps on the left, actions and bindings in the middle,
and the selected binding's properties on the right. A binding can be typed,
picked from a searchable list, or recorded with **Listen**. **Use as Project
Actions** writes `[input] actions` in the `.mproj`. The **Generate
AngelScript** option writes a namespace of action constants so a renamed
action fails to compile instead of silently doing nothing.

@subsection editor_lore Lore VCS

**Window > Lore VCS** shows the project's changes if the project is in a Lore
repository. It is optional; Mercury projects are ordinary folders and work
with any version control system.

@section editor_play Play, build and ship

**Project > Play / Stop** (F5) saves the map, compiles the scripts and starts
`mercury_player <project> --map <map>` as a separate process. The game's
output goes to the **Console**. There is no hot reload: stopping and playing
again starts a new process and a new game state.

**Project > Build Scripts** (F7) only compiles. Do this after changing a script
to refresh the script list in the Inspector.

**File > Build Game...** (Ctrl+B) writes a shippable folder. It reuses the
Release player (building one from source in a development editor), minifies
and compiles the scripts, and packs assets into compressed `.mpack` archives
instead of thousands of loose files:

@code{.text}
Builds/MyGame/MyGame          the game executable (mercury_player copy)
Builds/MyGame/engine.mpack    shaders, the default theme and fonts
Builds/MyGame/game.mpack      the project: map, assets, UI, scripts
Builds/MyGame/*.mindex        indexes that map a path to an archive and offset
@endcode

The dialog chooses where to write the build and how large each archive may be;
the output folder is remembered in the `.mproj` as `[build] output`. Run the
executable from the folder; if it finds `game.mpack` next to itself it runs
from the packs. See the project
<a href="md__d_o_c_u_m_e_n_t_a_t_i_o_n.html">DOCUMENTATION.md</a> for the packing
format and the macOS `.app` packaging script.

@section editor_shortcuts Keyboard shortcuts

| Shortcut | Action |
|---|---|
| Ctrl+N / Ctrl+O | New map / open map |
| Ctrl+S / Ctrl+Shift+S | Save / save map as |
| Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Shift+Z | Undo / redo |
| Ctrl+D / Delete | Duplicate / delete selected node |
| F5 | Play / stop |
| F7 | Build scripts |
| Ctrl+B | Build Game |
| W / E / R | Move / rotate / scale handles |
| Ctrl while dragging | Snap |
| F | Frame selection |
| Ctrl+Q | Exit |
| Ctrl+Space | Script completion (in the script editor) |

*/
